I didn't really use pets all that much until AFTER my first ascension.
Then again, I'm a bit weird :p

As for the armor, yes...you will get shouted at for suggesting that.
What you should have said is "put on every piece of UNCURSED armor you
find" The LAST thing a n00b needs is levi/fumbling they can't get rid
of!! You can test whether armor is cursed or not. The easiest method,
is if your pet walks on it. If there is no meat on the square, and the
pet happily steps onto it, or picks it up, then it is uncursed/blessed
and fine to be tried on. If you pet "moves reluctantly" or wont step
on that square at all, it's most likely cursed. This works well.
Another method (which will tell you the exact B/U/C status of an item)
is to drag it to an altar. Or leave it in a chest until you find an
altar. WARNING: DO NOT, I repeat NOT trust pet-testing on "conical
hat"

Couple of tips:

1) if you are a spellcaster (wizard, healer etc.) try to steer away
from metal armour, especially metal body armor. Use leather or DSM
instead (realistically leather early game, unless you get a wish early
on)
2) as a monk, avoid body armor in the early game ENITRELY or you'll
hit nothing
3) If you plan to melee stuff, then try to stay unburdened. That extra
hit the monster gets could be the difference between life and death.
4)Don't just drink from fountains. They can release some nasty
monsters
5) if you see an "n", and it is staying still, then move AROUND it. Do
NOT melee it. It can and will steal your items.
6)Don't melee little blue "e"s until you have a source of reflection!
Whilst they cannot harm you, they can freeze you, and other stuff can
come and kick your ass!
7)Try not to attack shopkeepers :)

Shujawa, if you use IRC, then connect on to the freenode network, and
join the channel #nethack. We're all relatively friendly. And don't
bite (much).
I may well add more to this list later, if I think of more.

Finally, my main tip. Don't get disheartened! It took me over 400
games before I first ascended. And having played over 200 since, I
still haven't done it again (although i've been trying stupid stuff
like conducted tourists etc.). Now, whilst it took me longer than most
to ascend (most likely due to not using pets), the moment you do, it's
worth all the YASDs!!

Enjoy =3DD


